{
  "about": [
    "link-rules-v1 (design 6.1, D13, D39). facts_cases: link_facts for one identity (Python, TR-10; materialized by TR-20/TR-23b).",
    "actionable_cases: link_actionable at judgment time with an explicit now (Python TR-10 and TS obs-link.ts, TR-24).",
    "Rows use state_rows.json field names; only the fields that decide a link are given. params are link-rules-v1's.",
    "input.pair, when absent, is default_pair: the two sets being paired (TR-20 passes the new set and the other channel's latest).",
    "Per country: a geo is paired through params.geo_country; t is the Trends row of that geo, G the GSC rows of that country.",
    "Only countries that params.geo_country pairs with a geo take part (PHL, IND only count in the site total).",
    "A Trends row flagged unstable voids the country. GSC rows flagged migration_suspect, mapping_changed, gap_exceeded or",
    "unverifiable are dropped; with degraded_no_country_24h, 24h rows of a country are ignored as if absent (not dropped).",
    "up(t) = rising and confirmed; low(t) = no row or state flat or sparse; gsc_up = a formal-admission row with a formal surge or",
    "from_zero label (24h) or rising label (7d); gsc_low = no row was dropped and no remaining row has any label.",
    "First match: cooling(t) -> cooling; up & gsc_up -> both_rising;",
    "up & gsc_low & page -> trends_lead_page; up & no page -> trends_lead_distribution; low & gsc_up -> site_only; else no fact.",
    "Referenced GSC row: the first gsc_up row, else the first row of G, ordered 24h then 7d. Global: up(WW) & gsc_up(ALL) ->",
    "global_parallel. When no country fact is both_rising but one country has up(t) and another has gsc_up, add different_markets.",
    "Anchors: trends_anchor is t's latest_block_end, else the set's; gsc_anchor is the referenced row's window_end, else the cutoff.",
    "pair_gap_minutes = |gsc_anchor - trends_anchor| (whole minutes, floor); timely = gap <= pair_max_gap_hours; published_gap_minutes",
    "= |gsc published_at - trends published_at| floor; stale = t carried_over or stale. Facts sort by country, null last.",
    "Actionability reasons, in order: label_not_actionable (global_parallel, different_markets), untimely_pair, stale_row,",
    "trends_set_too_old (now - trends published_at > 26 h), gsc_set_too_old (> 6 h). Exactly 26 h or 6 h still holds."
  ],
  "params": {
    "link_rules_version": "link-rules-v1",
    "pair_max_gap_hours": 48,
    "trends_max_age_hours": 26,
    "gsc_max_age_hours": 6,
    "geo_country": {
      "WW": "ALL",
      "US": "USA",
      "GB": "GBR",
      "ES": "ESP",
      "DE": "DEU",
      "FR": "FRA",
      "IT": "ITA",
      "MX": "MEX",
      "BR": "BRA",
      "BG": "BGR"
    },
    "up_labels": {"24h": ["surge", "from_zero"], "7d": ["rising"]},
    "low_states": ["flat", "sparse"],
    "excluded_flags": ["migration_suspect", "mapping_changed", "gap_exceeded", "unverifiable", "unstable"]
  },
  "default_pair": {
    "link_rules_version": "link-rules-v1",
